{
  "uid": "vitalcare-service-health",
  "title": "VitalCare \u2014 Service Health (PHI-free)",
  "description": "Aggregated operational metrics forwarded from the hospital OTel Collector. Contains no patient data.",
  "tags": [
    "hospital-remote",
    "vitalcare"
  ],
  "schemaVersion": 39,
  "version": 3,
  "editable": true,
  "graphTooltip": 1,
  "time": {
    "from": "now-15m",
    "to": "now"
  },
  "refresh": "30s",
  "templating": {
    "list": [
      {
        "name": "hospital_id",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
        },
        "query": "label_values(vitalcare_service_up, hospital_id)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true
      },
      {
        "name": "ward_id",
        "type": "query",
        "datasource": {
          "type": "prometheus",
          "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
        },
        "query": "label_values(vitalcare_service_up{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\"}, ward_id)",
        "refresh": 2,
        "includeAll": true,
        "multi": true
      }
    ]
  },
  "panels": [
    {
      "id": 0,
      "type": "text",
      "title": "How to read this dashboard",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 0
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "## VitalCare service health \u2014 remote view (PHI-free)\n\nThis dashboard shows the on-prem VitalCare service through a **narrow, aggregated, PHI-free metrics channel** forwarded from the hospital OTel Collector. No patient data ever reaches this dashboard.\n\n| If you see... | It means... | Do... |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| **Service Up** = 0 or missing | On-prem service is down OR the WAN connection to the hospital is down | Ping the on-prem contact. On-prem operators keep local visibility even when the cloud side is silent. |\n| **Error rate** yellow (>2%) or red (>5%) | Real processing errors in the ward | Contact the on-prem site. Read `Errors by class` for the class name \u2014 this is bounded and non-PHI. |\n| **Active Patients** dropped abruptly to 0 | Either the ward genuinely emptied, or the metric emitter crashed | Cross-check `Vitals received per second` \u2014 if that also dropped, it's the emitter. |\n| **PHI protection audit** table shows *any* unexpected label | \u26a0\ufe0f COMPLIANCE INCIDENT \u2014 the collector allow-list has drifted | Do not troubleshoot from this side. Escalate. See `docs/red-team.md`. |\n| Everything flat and green | \u2705 good state | Move on. |\n\n**Failure of this dashboard itself** (all panels no-data): usually a WAN outage, not a hospital-side problem. The collector's `sending_queue` will buffer through it \u2014 see `docs/offline-behavior.md`. The service is still safe; only *remote visibility* is degraded.\n\n**Never** ask the hospital to modify the clinical service to work around an observability problem. Observability failure must not cascade into patient-care failure. See `docs/network-boundary.md`."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 1,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Service Up",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "avg(vitalcare_service_up{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"})",
          "legendFormat": "up",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "colorMode": "background",
        "graphMode": "none",
        "textMode": "auto",
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        }
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "none",
          "min": 0,
          "max": 1,
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": 1
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Active Patients (aggregated)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 4,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(vitalcare_active_patient_count{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"})",
          "legendFormat": "patients",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "short"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "type": "stat",
      "title": "Error rate (last 5m)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 4,
        "w": 4,
        "x": 8,
        "y": 4
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum(rate(vitalcare_vitals_processing_errors_total{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"}[5m])) / clamp_min(sum(rate(vitalcare_vitals_received_total{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"}[5m])), 0.001)",
          "legendFormat": "error rate",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "reduceOptions": {
          "calcs": [
            "lastNotNull"
          ]
        },
        "graphMode": "area"
      },
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "percentunit",
          "thresholds": {
            "mode": "absolute",
            "steps": [
              {
                "color": "green",
                "value": null
              },
              {
                "color": "yellow",
                "value": 0.02
              },
              {
                "color": "red",
                "value": 0.05
              }
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Vitals received per second (by ward)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (hospital_id, ward_id) (rate(vitalcare_vitals_received_total{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"}[1m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{hospital_id}}/{{ward_id}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "reqps"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Processing latency (p50 / p95 / p99)",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 8
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.50, sum by (le) (rate(vitalcare_vitals_processing_duration_seconds_bucket{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p50",
          "refId": "A"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.95, sum by (le) (rate(vitalcare_vitals_processing_duration_seconds_bucket{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p95",
          "refId": "B"
        },
        {
          "expr": "histogram_quantile(0.99, sum by (le) (rate(vitalcare_vitals_processing_duration_seconds_bucket{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"}[5m])))",
          "legendFormat": "p99",
          "refId": "C"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "s"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "type": "timeseries",
      "title": "Errors by class",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 16
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "sum by (error_class) (rate(vitalcare_vitals_processing_errors_total{hospital_id=~\"$hospital_id\",ward_id=~\"$ward_id\"}[5m]))",
          "legendFormat": "{{error_class}}",
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "unit": "eps"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": 7,
      "type": "table",
      "title": "PHI protection audit \u2014 label allow-list only",
      "description": "This panel confirms that only the allow-listed labels appear on VitalCare metrics. If any unexpected label appears here, the OTel Collector allow-list is misconfigured \u2014 this is a compliance incident.",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 8,
        "w": 12,
        "x": 12,
        "y": 16
      },
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "hospital-cloud-prom"
      },
      "targets": [
        {
          "expr": "count by (__name__, hospital_id, ward_id, service_version, origin, collector_id) (vitalcare_vitals_received_total)",
          "format": "table",
          "instant": true,
          "refId": "A"
        }
      ],
      "options": {
        "showHeader": true
      }
    }
  ]
}